      "side": 1,
      "message": "Likely what is happening is that `kFloatConstant` has one reference to it (vardecl `const float kFloatConstantAlias \u003d kFloatConstant`). When we do dead-global elimination, we eliminate that reference. At that point, `kFloatConstant` drops to zero references, but we don\u0027t run the dead-global check a second time.\n\nPTAL\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/SkSLCompiler.cpp;l\u003d400;drc\u003d0cbf56d64706de13cc1d79fa708d4fbbfe77e21a\n\nTry changing this line to call `Transform::EliminateDeadGlobalVariables` in a loop until it returns false. Crib from here:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/sksl/SkSLCompiler.cpp;l\u003d337;drc\u003d0cbf56d64706de13cc1d79fa708d4fbbfe77e21a\n\nSee if that resolves it. I actually noticed this a while back, but we didn\u0027t have any test cases which changed when I added the loop, so I ignored it. The module minifier does have the loop because I wrote that more recently.",
      "parentUuid": "1f9b4e69_bce11c6a",
